\section{Related Work}
\label{sec:related_work}

We provide a detailed survey in Appendix~\ref{app:related_work}; here we position OntoCoDec along three axes.

\paragraph{Constrained decoding.}
XGrammar~\cite{dong2025xgrammar}, Outlines~\cite{willard2023outlines}, SynCode~\cite{ugare2024syncode}, SGLang~\cite{zheng2024sglang}, and related systems~\cite{beurer-kellner2023lmql,park2024grammar,jsonschemabench2025} enforce format validity via CFG-based token masking but lack cross-field semantic awareness.
PICARD~\cite{scholak2021picard} and \citet{pldi2025_type_constrained_codegen} compile type systems into prefix automata; KG-Trie~\cite{luo2025kgtrie} applies trie-based KG constraints during decoding for knowledge-to-text generation.
Unlike PICARD, which operates over a fixed, fully enumerated SQL schema with statically declared column types, OntoCoDec's entity registry is populated dynamically during generation as entity spans are extracted from free text, requiring prefix-decidable enforcement rather than context-free lookup.

\paragraph{Schema-aware IE.}
GoLLIE~\cite{sainz2024gollie}, KnowCoder~\cite{knowcoder_acl2024}, and others~\cite{guidex2025,josifoski2022genie,paolini2021tanl,cabot2021rebel,wang2023instructuie,qi2024adelie,fei2022lasuie,lu2022uie,zhou2024universalner} encode ontology structure via training-time internalization without runtime enforcement~\cite{wadhwa2023revisiting}.
GoLLIE achieves schema compliance through annotation-guideline-guided generation at training time (reporting 63.6--70.1\% RE F1 on ACE05 in supervised settings; SciERC RE not evaluated); OntoCoDec provides orthogonal runtime enforcement, composable with any generative IE system including GoLLIE itself (Appendix~\ref{app:gollie-comparison}).

\paragraph{Constraint enforcement in IE.}
\citet{roth_yih_2004} and \citet{riedel2010modeling} formulated hard type constraints via integer linear programming (ILP); post-hoc validation~\cite{khorshidi2025odke,spires_2024,ontologx_2025} detects violations after generation but discards up to 74\% of predictions.
EnriCo~\cite{zaratiana2024enrico} uses answer set programming (ASP); IterGen~\cite{ugare2025itergen} backtracks on violations; \citet{vukovic2024dialogue} combines ontology constraints with constrained chain-of-thought for dialogue RE---OntoCoDec uses forward-only masking at $O(|V|)$ per step without iterative refinement.
Grammar-only enforcement (GCD~\cite{geng2023gcd}, BoostCD~\cite{boostcd2025}) achieves only 3\% DR reduction (\S\ref{sec:constrained-baselines}).

